WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.810
It was the navy's Fleet Week.

2
00:00:02.811 --> 00:00:06.527
The bay was full of ships for people to see and visit.

3
00:00:06.528 --> 00:00:11.972
Orson stood with his cousin Nick on top of a long black submarine.

4
00:00:11.973 --> 00:00:16.380
Nick was a sailor who worked aboard this underwater vessel.

5
00:00:16.381 --> 00:00:20.613
"What does this submarine do?" Orson asked.

6
00:00:20.614 --> 00:00:25.224
"The navy uses submarines to help protect our country," Nick said.

7
00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:29.867
"Most of our missions are for military research. Ready to see inside?"

8
00:00:29.868 --> 00:00:33.992
Orson shivered. The sub had no windows.

9
00:00:33.993 --> 00:00:36.240
It seemed scary.

10
00:00:36.241 --> 00:00:42.706
Nick climbed down the ladder inside the hatch, the round opening that led into the sub.

11
00:00:42.707 --> 00:00:45.989
"Come on down," he called.

12
00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:50.564
Orson cautiously stepped onto the ladder's first rung.

13
00:00:50.565 --> 00:00:53.816
"Will the sub sink while we're on board?"

14
00:00:53.817 --> 00:01:00.072
"Subs control when they submerge," Nick assured him as they climbed down the ladder.

15
00:01:00.073 --> 00:01:03.888
"Tanks filled with air help them float.

16
00:01:03.889 --> 00:01:07.299
To submerge, we pump water into the tanks.

17
00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:11.351
That makes the sub heavier, so it goes down."

18
00:01:11.352 --> 00:01:14.591
"How does it get back up?"

19
00:01:14.592 --> 00:01:19.011
"We fill the tanks with air again to make it float."

20
00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:23.078
Nick grinned at him. "We won't submerge today."

21
00:01:23.079 --> 00:01:26.346
Orson reached the bottom of the ladder.

22
00:01:26.347 --> 00:01:28.834
"Why is it so cramped in here?

23
00:01:28.835 --> 00:01:32.250
The sub looks huge on the outside."

24
00:01:32.251 --> 00:01:34.772
"Nuclear subs are big.

25
00:01:34.773 --> 00:01:41.563
This one is over ninety meters long, but the power plant and equipment take up most of the space," said Nick.

26
00:01:41.564 --> 00:01:45.761
"The 135 crew members get any room that's left."

27
00:01:45.762 --> 00:01:52.716
He laughed. "Some subs, like the ones they use for scientific research, are powered with oil.

28
00:01:52.717 --> 00:01:56.913
Oil-powered subs must surface every few days.

29
00:01:56.914 --> 00:02:02.211
Nuclear subs can stay underwater for months."

30
00:02:02.212 --> 00:02:06.737
"Don't you run out of water and air when the sub stays underwater that long?"

31
00:02:06.738 --> 00:02:10.339
"We make our own fresh water and air."

32
00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:13.992
"We made fresh water in school!" Orson said.

33
00:02:13.993 --> 00:02:19.791
"We boiled salt water and saved the condensed steam. Is that what you do?"

34
00:02:19.792 --> 00:02:22.879
"Exactly," said Nick.

35
00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:27.921
"We make enough water for crew members to drink and take a three-minute shower every day.

36
00:02:27.922 --> 00:02:31.604
Most of the water, though, is used to cool equipment."

37
00:02:31.605 --> 00:02:34.301
"How do you make air?"

38
00:02:34.302 --> 00:02:37.184
"We take oxygen from water.

39
00:02:37.185 --> 00:02:42.592
And we can reuse existing air by getting rid of the carbon dioxide people breathe out."

40
00:02:42.593 --> 00:02:45.351
"Cool," Orson said.

41
00:02:45.352 --> 00:02:49.741
Nick led Orson through rooms filled with computers.

42
00:02:49.742 --> 00:02:55.097
"We navigate with GPS on the surface, but GPS doesn't work underwater.

43
00:02:55.098 --> 00:02:59.456
So we navigate by keeping track of our direction and speed."

44
00:02:59.457 --> 00:03:03.745
"How do you keep the sub from crashing into things?"

45
00:03:03.746 --> 00:03:08.113
"We use sound. We listen for sounds from other ships.

46
00:03:08.114 --> 00:03:10.999
We also use a device called sonar.

47
00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:15.095
It bounces sound off objects to detect and locate them."

48
00:03:15.096 --> 00:03:18.855
"That's what dolphins do!" Orson said.

49
00:03:18.856 --> 00:03:21.836
They climbed down a narrow stairway.

50
00:03:21.837 --> 00:03:26.303
Here beds were stacked three-high along the walls.

51
00:03:26.304 --> 00:03:28.901
"This is the crew's quarters."

52
00:03:28.902 --> 00:03:32.387
Nick pointed to a small drawer under one bed.

53
00:03:32.388 --> 00:03:34.914
"I keep all my stuff here."

54
00:03:34.915 --> 00:03:41.165
"Everything?" Orson had a room full of stuff at home.

55
00:03:41.166 --> 00:03:44.264
"What do you do all day?"

56
00:03:44.265 --> 00:03:46.667
"I'm on watch for eight hours.

57
00:03:46.668 --> 00:03:49.338
That's when I'm helping to operate the sub.

58
00:03:49.339 --> 00:03:53.826
When I'm not on watch, I still have to work to help clean and maintain the sub.

59
00:03:53.827 --> 00:03:56.531
We get some free time too.

60
00:03:56.532 --> 00:03:59.829
Then I sleep for eight hours."

61
00:03:59.830 --> 00:04:03.167
Suddenly the sub rocked.

62
00:04:03.168 --> 00:04:06.377
"Whoa!" Orson said.

63
00:04:06.378 --> 00:04:09.313
"Don't worry," Nick said.

64
00:04:09.314 --> 00:04:14.703
"Waves rock subs on the surface, but it's smooth sailing underwater."

65
00:04:14.704 --> 00:04:18.119
"I believe you." Orson smiled.

66
00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:22.008
"Living underwater seems like living in a spaceship!

67
00:04:22.009 --> 00:04:26.463
But I think I like living on land better!"

